Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- reproducable on 4.6 dev 4\n- still working on 4.5 stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.dev4 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1660 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8157) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 15.92 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nSetting a RichTextLabels size to the size returned by Font.get_multiline_string_size() previously would have the text perfectly fit. In the latest release this is no longer the case, instead \n| Header | Header |\n|--------|--------|\n| 4.5.Stable | 4.6 dev4 |\n| <img width=\"232\" height=\"84\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9a5e6275-198e-4c46-a6a4-6140e45a9fb3\" /> | <img width=\"181\" height=\"59\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0a5f09b0-1683-4bcb-bba1-ce0780d54b31\" />| \n\nOn the same code:\n```gdscript\n\t%RTL.text = \"Waiting for Godot\"\n\tvar font: Font = %RTL.get_theme_font(&\"normal_font\")\n\tvar text_size = font.get_multiline_string_size(\n\t\t%RTL.get_parsed_text(),\n\t\tHORIZONTAL_ALIGNMENT_LEFT,\n\t\tmax_width,\n\t\t%RTL.get_theme_font_size(&\"normal_font_size\")\n\t\t)\n\n\t%RTL.size = text_size\n```\nAlternatively this could imply an issue with the get_multiline_string function, not sure, it does return the same values in both versions though.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUse the code above, no special setup needed. Or try the MRP.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp-rtl-size-change.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23863023/mrp-rtl-size-change.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Jowan-Spooner","id":42868150,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyODY4MTUw",